WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.700
This video concerns the events in Ukraine,
especially the history being used by Putin

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.200
to justify the invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.530
As a historian that also happens to be from
Eastern Europe (or Central Europe depending

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:17.440
on how you choose to define it), I have, in
recent weeks, been asked on numerous occasions

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.720
by friends, family, and strangers to explain
the historical statements made by Putin to

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.300
justify his war.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.750
Many other historians have lately been in
the same position and, therefore, I think

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.430
it would be prudent to make a quick video
addressing all of this.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:37.690
To help convey some basic facts about Ukrainian
and Russian history and to show how these

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:41.109
facts are being altered by Putin to fit his
agenda.

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:47.600
In 2021 Putin wrote an essay titled On the
Historical Unity of Russians and Ukrainians

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.589
which, to summarize, basically gave multiple
historical justifications to the idea that

00:00:52.589 --> 00:00:56.300
Ukranians are Russians and Ukraine belongs
with Russia.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:02.210
This goes hand in hand with his previous statements
about Ukraine in 2014, or with his various

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.080
speeches in 2022.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.090
The idea that Ukranians and Russians are basically
the same people is by far not a new one and

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:14.420
it had existed in nationalistic Russian circles,
in one way or another, for centuries.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:18.970
To explain all of this, however, one has to
start with the polity that all modern Eastern

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.030
Slavic nations trace their national, and often
ethnic, origins to.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:24.030
The Kievan Rus’.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:29.030
The Kievan Rus’ was an early medieval eastern
european polity existing roughly from the

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:32.190
late 9th century, centered around the city
of Kyiv.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:36.600
I have already addressed the formation and
history of the Kievan Rus in my video on Early

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.450
East Slavic History, so I won’t talk about
it in detail here.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:45.030
But, the important factor to comment on here
is that it would be wholly inappropriate to

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:50.120
talk of the Kievan Rus’ as Russian, or Ukrainian,
or purely Slavic.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.810
The Kievan Rus’, just like many other early
medieval polities, was a multiethnic kingdom

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.560
composed of many different people groups.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.960
There were Vikings from today’s Sweden called
Varangians, there where various Finno-Ugric

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.890
tribes, various Eurasian Turkic, Iranian,
and other nomadic tribes, there was a Jewish

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:12.609
community of traders, and even the various
Eastern Slavic tribes ,which were the majority

00:02:12.609 --> 00:02:16.629
population of the Kievan Rus’, saw themselves
as different from each other.

00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:21.100
There did not exist some kind of an universal
Eastern Slavic kinship (affinity), Slavic

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:25.819
tribes were just as likely to fight each other
as they were to fight other people.

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:30.219
Kievan Rus’ would eventually fall in the
first half of the 13th century due to internal

00:02:30.219 --> 00:02:34.560
fracturing and power struggles and external
invasion by the Mongols.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.099
Therefore, speaking of the Kievan Rus’ as
anything else than the product of its time,

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:44.470
a kingdom of many, often bickering Eastern
Slavic tribes, a kingdom comprised of multitude

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:49.860
of different peoples, a kingdom which slowly
fractured apart and was conquered by the Mongols,

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.689
would be inappropriate if not outright wrong.

00:02:53.689 --> 00:02:58.310
In the 14th century and a bit in the 15th
century, most of what is today’s Ukraine,

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:01.620
including Kyiv, was conquered by Poland and
Lithuania.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:07.020
For the next roughly 400 years these lands
evolved and developed in culture, language,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.740
art, etc. under Polish and Lithuanian control.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.150
During the same time the Mongols, or as they
came to be known in Eastern Europe, the Golden

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:19.459
Horde, remained in control roughly east of
the Dnieper bend.

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:24.599
Here the Mongols exerted power over the local
population and enforced tribute payments from

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:27.150
the various local towns and villages.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.780
One of these towns was a wooden trading post
on the banks of the Moskva River, known as

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.169
Moscow.

00:03:33.169 --> 00:03:38.189
Moscow over time became the center of an increasingly
powerful principality which bore the name

00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:40.670
of its capital city Muscovy.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:44.999
Muscovy eventually grew more powerful than
their Mongol overlords and through a series

00:03:44.999 --> 00:03:48.459
of conflicts became independent in 1480.

00:03:48.459 --> 00:03:53.420
From there Muscovy grew more and more powerful
with ever expanding military conquests.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:59.590
With this expansion Muscovy began to style
itself more and more as a kingdom of not a

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.680
Rus’ people but of the Rus’ people.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:08.069
To explain, since the time of the Kievan Rus’
the word Rus’ was just used to identify

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:09.610
all Eastern Slavs.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:15.079
It wasn’t supposed to denote any single
Slavic peoples, it was used just as a classification

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:17.329
for all Eastern Slavic people.

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:22.990
In essence the words Eastern Slavs today are
used the same way the word Rus’ was used

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:23.990
back then.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:29.260
So Muscovy’s increasing styling of itself
as the nation of all the Rus’ meant that

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:34.639
they began to create an idea that all Eastern
Slavs belong under their control.

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:39.479
This is evident, for example, when in the
16th century Ivan the Terrible, following

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:44.770
in his grandfather's footsteps, assumed the
title of “Tsar and Grand Duke of all Rus'”.

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:51.169
No longer was Muscovi just Muscovi, a Duchy
of a single Rus' peoples, it was now the Tsardom

00:04:51.169 --> 00:04:57.091
of Russia, literally meaning the Empire of
all Rus’ people or, in other words, all

00:04:57.091 --> 00:04:58.720
Eastern Slavs.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.729
This way, the country that over time just
became known as Russia, could start to justify

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:08.560
wars with their western neighbors in the name
of unifying all the Rus’.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:14.340
Even if all the Rus’, or all Eastern Slavs,
did not and still do not see themselves as

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:19.889
the same people just like, for example, all
west Germanic speakers don’t necessarily

00:05:19.889 --> 00:05:22.340
see themselves as all the same people.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:28.759
By Muscovy styling itself as a polity of all
the Rus’, as Russia or Russia, it harkened

00:05:28.759 --> 00:05:33.470
back to the kingdom of the Kievan Rus’ and
its historical borders.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:38.530
Muscovite Russia went to great lengths to
try to convince people of Kievan Rus’ Muscovite

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:43.410
Russian continuity, even though, as we discussed,
talking about the Kievan Rus in any other

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:48.030
context than it being a product of its time
which got conquered by the Mongols would be

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.060
wholly inaccurate.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:54.340
So, when Putin talks of Ukraine as a place
where Russia began on account of the Kievan

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:58.870
Rus’, and, therefore, should be part of
today’s Russia; he is talking about a made

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:04.040
up Muscovite Russian concept that regards
modern Russia as the successor to the Kievan

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:08.189
Rus’ which has no actual basis in history.

00:06:08.189 --> 00:06:13.530
Early Modern Russia slowly, in multiple wars
and partitions between the mid 17th and early

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:18.880
19th century, conquered most, but not all,
the lands of today's Ukraine and Belarus away

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.069
from the Polish Lithuanian Commonwealth.

00:06:21.069 --> 00:06:26.530
Russia was hoping to assimilate all these
newly conquered Eastern Slavs into their idealized

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:31.310
pan-Russian nation, despite many of these
Eastern Slavs often having a different language

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:35.970
to the Muscovite Russians, different culture,
and different costumes, as they were influenced

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:40.840
by the Poles, Lithuanians, and overall more
western ideology for centuries.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:45.691
These people were still Eastern Slavs, and
they still saw themselves as the Rus’, but

00:06:45.691 --> 00:06:50.069
not as Muscovite Rus’ or, in other words,
as Russians.

00:06:50.069 --> 00:06:55.300
Therefore when Putin in his speech on the
21st of February 2022 stated that “For a

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:59.750
long time, the inhabitants of the historical
lands of the South-West of Ancient Russia

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.659
called themselves Russians and Orthodox.

00:07:02.659 --> 00:07:07.400
This was the case until the 17th century,
when part of these territories were reunified

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.350
with the Russian state.” he was wrong.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:15.920
These people identified as the Rus’, as
the Eastern Slavs, but not as Russians; and

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:20.539
ever since the word Rus’ got appropriated
by the Muscovite Russians, the people living

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:23.879
in today’s Ukraine had to start using other
identifiers.

00:07:23.879 --> 00:07:26.469
Like, for example, Ukranians.

00:07:26.469 --> 00:07:30.620
The name of Ukraine existed far before this
time but it was around this time it got more

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:35.400
widely adopted due to the appropriation of
the name Rus’ by the people from Muscovy

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.060
by the Russians.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:42.000
Despite all these factors, Russia tried very
hard, through Russification, to assimilate

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:47.499
all the Eastern Slavs into what they called
the obshcherusskii narod, meaning one Russian

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:53.139
peoples, to them all the Eastern Slavs, all
the Rus’, were the same people and, therefore,

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:57.220
they should all be talking and acting as the
same people.

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:02.879
In some areas this Russification proved to
be successful, for example, almost all Ukrainian

00:08:02.879 --> 00:08:07.439
high nobility assimilated into the Russian
aristocracy by the 19th century.

00:08:07.439 --> 00:08:12.800
However, in other areas, this Russification
backfired and, in opposition to it, during

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:18.410
the late 18th and 19th century, Ukrainian
national consciousness consolidated more thoroughly

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:23.020
and Ukrainian language was officially codified
by Ukrainian intellectuals.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:28.830
The continued survival of this Ukrainian national
consciousness in the 19th century proved extremely

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.949
problematic to the Russian government.

00:08:30.949 --> 00:08:33.339
The Russian minister of interior P.A.

00:08:33.339 --> 00:08:39.010
Valuev said in 1876 that “permitting the
creation of a special literature for the common

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:44.540
people in the Ukrainian dialect would signify
collaborating in the alienation of Ukraine

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:49.139
from the rest of Russia … To permit the
separation of thirteen million Little Russians

00:08:49.139 --> 00:08:54.810
(That is what the Russians called Ukranians)
would be the utmost political irresponsibility,

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:59.870
especially in view of the unifying movement
which is proceeding alongside us among the

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:00.890
Germanic tribes.”

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:06.940
In heed of this warning the Tsar forbade all,
with very few exceptions, literary publications

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.310
and teaching in Ukrainian.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:13.649
The Russian empire also conducted a series
of forced relocations and overall sometimes

00:09:13.649 --> 00:09:16.870
violent suppression of Ukrainian people.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:21.810
Many Ukrainian thinkers, therefore, fled to
Western Ukraine which was part of the Habsburg

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:22.810
Monarchy.

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:27.360
Here Ukrainian culture and language wasn’t
suppressed as much, and, infact, it was seen

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:32.000
by the Austrians as a beneficial counterbalance
to the Poles living in Austria.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.800
Therefore, much of Ukrainian literature of
the late 19th century came from Western Ukraine

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:41.500
and this literature was often smuggled into
Russian controlled Ukraine which continued

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:45.630
to be under harsh Russification pressure well
into the first world war.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:50.440
The Russian Empire lost the First World and
in the aftermath of this loss Russia fell

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.840
into Civil war.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:56.670
Putin, again in his 21st of February speech
stated that “modern Ukraine was fully and

00:09:56.670 --> 00:10:01.690
completely created by Russia, more precisely,
Bolshevik and communist Russia.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:07.160
This process began almost immediately after
the revolution of 1917, and Lenin and his

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:12.790
associates did it in a way that was extremely
harsh on Russia - separating, uprooting part

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.850
of its own historical territories.

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:18.470
Nobody asked the millions of people living
there what they thought”.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:24.730
Now, taking aside the fact that, as we discussed,
Ukranians and Ukrainian identity existed far

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:30.600
before 1917, some key events did happen during
this time and they did not happen the way

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.280
Putin described them.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:37.510
When Russia lost the first world war to the
Central Powers in 1917, most of the area of

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:41.199
what is today Ukraine fell under the control
of the Germans and Austro-Hungarians.

00:10:41.199 --> 00:10:47.000
However, these countries never really had
time to consolidate power in this region and

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.360
both soon surrendered to the allies.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:54.380
Therefore, there was a large powervacume in
Ukraine and so many different factions started

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.900
to vie for control.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:11:00.290
The most successful of these factions was
the Ukrainian People's Republic established

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.029
by the Ukrainian Directorate.

00:11:02.029 --> 00:11:07.420
The Ukrainian People's Republic would, in
1920, symbolically unify with the West Ukrainian

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:12.019
People's Republic which was established in
the Ukrainian lands formerly controlled by

00:11:12.019 --> 00:11:13.019
Austria-Hungary.

00:11:13.019 --> 00:11:18.529
This idea of a finally unified Ukrainian state,
however, never really came to fruition as

00:11:18.529 --> 00:11:23.690
the Ukrainians who sought independence had
to fight many other groups, like Ukranians

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:28.199
who didn’t want independence, or Poles,
or White Russians, or the Ukrainian Soviet

00:11:28.199 --> 00:11:33.480
Socialist Republic which was created and supported
by the Russian Bolsheviks, etc.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:38.490
This entire complicated situation ended in
the 1920s when the West Ukrainian People’s

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:43.240
Republic was conquered by the Poles, and the
Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic, with

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:48.030
the help from the Russian Bolsheviks, won
the Ukrainian civil war against the Ukrainian

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:50.820
People's Republic, and other Ukrainian factions.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:56.360
As you can see Ukraine wasn’t created by
Lenin in 1917, there where genuent tries to

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:01.589
form an independent state of Ukraine in the
post war period which, in the end, failed

00:12:01.589 --> 00:12:03.019
on account of the Bolsheviks.

00:12:03.019 --> 00:12:08.029
“Nobody asked the millions of people living
there what they thought” because what many

00:12:08.029 --> 00:12:11.649
of them thought was that they wanted an independent
Ukraine.

00:12:11.649 --> 00:12:16.630
The mere fact that Lenin along with the Bolsheviks
established the Ukrainian Soviet Socialist

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:21.040
Republic shows just how different Ukrainians
were to Russians.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:25.760
The Russian Bolsheviks simply couldn’t have
controlled Ukraine by merely annexing it.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:31.290
The Bolsheviks had to establish and support
an internal Bolshevik movement within Ukraine

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:33.329
in order to gain control of it.

00:12:33.329 --> 00:12:37.580
After winning the Ukrainian civil war with
the help from the red army the Ukrainian Soviet

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:40.250
Socialist Republic joined the USSR.

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:45.459
The way the new Russian Soviet state was going
to be run was a matter of STRONG debate among

00:12:45.459 --> 00:12:46.570
the Bolsheviks.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.779
In the end a federative solution was chosen.

00:12:48.779 --> 00:12:54.000
In accordance with this solution a “People's
Commissariat of Nationalities”, or just

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:59.230
Narkomnats for short, was created; whose job
was to make the most accurate federale divisions

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:04.070
within the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics,
or just USSR for short.

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:09.010
It is this body that Putin refers to when
he talks about “What was the point of transferring

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:15.100
to the newly, often arbitrarily formed administrative
units – the union republics – vast territories

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:17.050
that had nothing to do with them?”

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:22.700
But this is inaccurate, as Geoffrey Hosking
states in in his book Russia and the Russians,

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:28.440
“They [the Narkomnats] drew on censuses,
historical studies, and ethnographic, geographic,

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:34.290
and linguistic surveys to try to determine
as accurately as possible the ethnic composition

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:38.850
and degree of the national development of
the territories over which the soviet state

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.449
was assuming sovereignty.”

00:13:40.449 --> 00:13:45.649
They were definitely not creating “arbitrarily
formed administrative units”.

00:13:45.649 --> 00:13:51.980
With that said, as Lenin died and Stalin took
control over the USSR, things changed.

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:56.590
For one, a more direct centralization of power
occurred and the “Russian Soviet Federative

00:13:56.590 --> 00:14:01.850
Socialist Republic” or just Russia for short,
which was the largest and most dominant political

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:07.589
power in the USSR, came to, for all intents
and purposes, dominate the whole of USSR and

00:14:07.589 --> 00:14:09.750
all its other constituents.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:15.750
In the context of centralizing power, in Ukraine
specifically, Stalin’s infamous purges often

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:21.100
targeted the Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic
as one of his “principal aims was to disrupt

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:26.600
ethnic patronage systems and break down local
resistance to orders from Moscow.”

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:31.589
On top of that his economic reforms caused
one of the worst famines in history called

00:14:31.589 --> 00:14:37.810
the holodomor which disproportionately affected
minorities in the USSR like the Ukrainians,

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.790
Khazaks, Tatars, etc.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.970
There were also many killings, imprisonments,
and forced resettlements of Ukranians who

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:46.700
refused to comply with the Soviet state.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:51.519
The Western Ukranians in Poland were faring
slightly better than their eastern counterparts

00:14:51.519 --> 00:14:53.630
but not by a lot.

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:57.830
Ukranians were often looked down upon by the
Poles especially after Poland had to fight

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:02.389
the West Ukrainian People's Republic over
land which the Poles deemed as rightfully

00:15:02.389 --> 00:15:03.389
theirs.

00:15:03.389 --> 00:15:08.000
Due to this negative Ukrainian sentiment in
Poland many laws were created that hindered

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:13.709
Ukrainian social development and resettled
Polish farmers in areas populated by a Ukrainian

00:15:13.709 --> 00:15:14.709
majority.

00:15:14.709 --> 00:15:20.980
All this resulted in that, when WW2 started
and the Nazis began to occupy Eastern Europe,

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:24.259
Ukranians welcomed the Germans as their liberators.

00:15:24.259 --> 00:15:28.569
Putin referred to this in his declaration
of war speech stating that “They (the Ukranians)

00:15:28.569 --> 00:15:33.910
will undoubtedly try to bring war to Crimea
just as they have done in Donbass, to kill

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:39.470
innocent people just as members of the punitive
units of Ukrainian nationalists and Hitler’s

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:42.360
accomplices did during the Great Patriotic
War.”

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:45.810
This statement, again, is not completely true.

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:50.779
Yes, Ukrainians did initially welcome the
Germans as liberators, and yes there where

00:15:50.779 --> 00:15:55.640
Ukranians who collaborated and helped the
Nazis but that isn’t the full picture.

00:15:55.640 --> 00:16:00.790
For one, every occupied country in Europe
had some Nazi colaboraters.

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:04.500
The French, the Slovaks, the Czechs, the Poles
even though they like to deny it, and even

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:07.620
the Russians all had Nazi collaborators.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:12.839
However, these collaborators do not represent
the majority of the population in these countries.

00:16:12.839 --> 00:16:18.360
The initial Ukrainian sentiment towards the
Germans as their liberators quickly faded

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:23.569
away as it became clear that the Nazis saw
the Ukranians, along with other Slavs, as

00:16:23.569 --> 00:16:27.120
inferior human beings, as Untermenschen.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:32.250
Reichskommissar Erich Koch, who was in charge
of governing occupied Ukraine, stated “There

00:16:32.250 --> 00:16:34.920
is no such thing as a free Ukraine.

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:38.730
Our aim is to ensure that Ukrainians work
for Germany.”

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:44.120
To this aim “Abled-bodied men and women,
including adolescents, were rounded up and

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:47.949
deported to work as slaves in German factories
and mines.

00:16:47.949 --> 00:16:51.259
Anyone who resisted was publicly hanged as
an example.

00:16:51.259 --> 00:16:56.310
Several million citizens of the occupied regions
[of the USSR] worked for or collaborated with

00:16:56.310 --> 00:17:01.690
the Germans, either as soldiers or as civilians,
but that was usually because the alternative

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:03.920
was violent death.”

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:08.839
Many Ukrainians became sick of being occupied
by the Poles, the Russians, and the Nazis

00:17:08.839 --> 00:17:14.339
and formed partisan groups which at their
height consistet of over 100 thousand people.

00:17:14.339 --> 00:17:19.689
These partisan groups were often loosely unified
and some groups waged guerrilla warfare against

00:17:19.689 --> 00:17:24.949
all occupiers like Poles, Soviets, and Germans
while others collaborated with one of the

00:17:24.949 --> 00:17:26.959
factions against the other ones.

00:17:26.959 --> 00:17:30.559
Flip flopping between the factions was also
not uncommon.

00:17:30.559 --> 00:17:35.460
The goal of all these partisan groups was
to create, in one way or another, some kind

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:37.970
of an independent state of Ukraine.

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:42.733
To achieve this goal they fought with sometimes
inexcusable brutality with SOME (but not all)

00:17:42.733 --> 00:17:45.510
partisan groups conducting ethnic cleansing.

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:50.430
Some of these partisan groups continued to
operate after the war ended, fighting well

00:17:50.430 --> 00:17:52.390
into the 1950s.

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:57.090
So when Putin stated in his declaration of
war speech “that the people living in territories

00:17:57.090 --> 00:18:01.220
which are part of today’s Ukraine were not
asked how they want to build their lives when

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:04.580
the USSR was created or after World War II.”

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:08.429
they were not asked because they didn’t
want to be part of the USSR.

00:18:08.429 --> 00:18:14.850
In both instances, as we saw, there was active
military opposition to Russian, and other

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:15.850
countries’, rule in Ukraine.

00:18:15.850 --> 00:18:20.030
After the second world war ended Ukraine was
subject to harsh crackdowns by the Soviets

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:25.679
including imprisonments, killings, deportations,
etc. as they retaliated against the actions

00:18:25.679 --> 00:18:27.780
of the Ukrainian partisans.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:33.039
When it comes to Crimea, this area was historically
inhabited by the Tatars, a turkic language

00:18:33.039 --> 00:18:34.290
speaking peoples.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:39.950
However, by the end of WW2 they were dubiously
charged with supporting the Nazis and where

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:42.809
either killed or deported to mostly Khazakstan.

00:18:42.809 --> 00:18:48.900
The depopulated Crimea was then resettled
by some Ukranians but mostly Russians.

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:54.300
So when Putin talks of Crimea as being Russian,
it's only Russian because most of its indigenous

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:57.270
Tatar population was killed or deported.

00:18:57.270 --> 00:19:02.669
Crimea was originally under Russian control
but it was then given to Ukraine in 1954 by

00:19:02.669 --> 00:19:03.669
Krushchev.

00:19:03.669 --> 00:19:08.260
There are multiple reasons as to why Krushchev
gave Crimea to Ukraine but ultimately the

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:11.350
most important factor was that it did not
matter.

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:15.590
Crimea was still in the USSR just under a
slightly different administration.

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:19.610
As William Taubman states, Krushchev never
even thought of the future ramifications of

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:23.920
such a decision as he most likely couldn’t
have imagined a future where Ukraine would

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:27.220
not be part of some kind of a Russian state.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:31.990
With all that said, after the death of Stalin,
the cold war period finally brought some relief

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:33.020
to Ukraine.

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:38.580
This is not to say that Russification efforts
went away, no, but they did become more passive.

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:43.659
For example, like giving preferential treatment
in the government or the work place to Russian

00:19:43.659 --> 00:19:46.260
speakers over Ukrainian speakers.

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:50.690
Active Russification, like the aforementioned
resettlement of Ukrainians, became, largely,

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:52.560
a thing of the past.

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:57.470
Although, with that said, any kind of formation
of nationlistic Ukrainian movements during

00:19:57.470 --> 00:20:00.490
this time was still harshly cracked down upon.

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:03.810
Ukraine during this time also saw large-scale
industrialization.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:07.950
This industrialization was often followed
with an influx of Russian migrant workers

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:11.990
mostly to cities like Kyiv, Luhanks, Kharkiv,
etc.

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:18.070
This, along with the centuries long Russification
efforts, meant that Ukraine, by 1990, had

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:21.090
a sizable native Russian speaking population.

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:27.360
Native Russian speaking, however, did not
and still does not always mean Russian identifying.

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:33.830
There are plenty of native Russian speakers
in Ukraine that identify as Urkanians and

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:36.630
the majority of Ukranians can speak Russian.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:43.320
By one 2010 poll, 76% of Ukrainian citizens
could speak Russian despite only around 17.2%

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:46.470
of citizens identifying as Russian.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:51.120
When it came to the breakup of the USSR the
Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic, under

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:56.080
pressure from its citizens, declared independence
in August of 1991.

00:20:56.080 --> 00:21:01.320
That same year, in December, the new country
of just Ukraine held an independence referendum.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:09.310
The voter turnout was 84.2%, and out of those
people 92.3% voted for independence.

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:15.370
There wasn’t a single county, or Oblast,
that had an anti-independence majority, even

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:20.240
Crimea, the oblast with the largest percentage
of native Russian speakers, voted in favor

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:24.260
of independence with a voter turnout of 60%.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:29.870
On top of that Ukraine along with USA, UK
and Russia signed the Budapest Memorandum

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:31.500
in 1994.

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:36.710
This treaty guaranteed to the new country
of Ukraine that the other signatory countries

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:41.539
“reaffirm their commitment to Ukraine … to
respect the independence and sovereignty and

00:21:41.539 --> 00:21:42.920
the existing borders of Ukraine.”

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:48.220
and that they also “reaffirm their obligation
to refrain from the threat or use of force

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:53.010
against the territorial integrity or political
independence of Ukraine, and that none of

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:56.179
their weapons will ever be used against Ukraine”.

00:21:56.179 --> 00:22:00.520
All of this in exchange for Ukraine giving
up its nuclear weapons which it inherited

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:09.210
after the breakup of the USSR.

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:14.220
With that said, this newfound independence
did not mean Ukraine was completely leaving

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:15.730
Russia behind.

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:19.950
Ukraine still remained a close ally of Russia
for the next couple of decades.

00:22:19.950 --> 00:22:23.880
However, a slow change started to happen in
the 21st century.

00:22:23.880 --> 00:22:29.520
A large majority of Ukrainian people increasingly
started to look westewards while some Ukrainians,

00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:34.720
and especially Russian leaders, wanted Ukraine
to remain a close ally of Russia, just like

00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:35.890
BelaRus did.

00:22:35.890 --> 00:22:41.210
These divisions of opinion then lead to all
the events that occurred in 2014 and are happening

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:42.210
now.

00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:44.950
Lastly, I will talk about languages in Ukraine.

00:22:44.950 --> 00:22:50.169
The language laws that have been adopted by
Ukraine since the 2014 crises have been swayed

00:22:50.169 --> 00:22:53.169
by increasing Ukranian nationalistic sentiment.

00:22:53.169 --> 00:22:58.910
The threat of Russia in the 2014 crisis made
Ukraine rethink it’s quite by-lingual stans

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:05.809
on the Russian and Ukrainian languages, after
all as stated before 76% of Ukranians could

00:23:05.809 --> 00:23:11.660
speak Russian, and Russian was still sometimes
used by ethnic Ukranians for communication.

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:16.670
However, the increasing threat of Russia to
Ukraine made the use of Russian fall out of

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:23.200
favor, and, therefore, its language status
became increasingly sidelined in favor of

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:24.200
Ukrainian.

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:30.609
With three controversial language bills passing
in 2014, 2017, and 2019.

00:23:30.609 --> 00:23:35.420
Despite Putin's claims “to protect people
who have been subjected to bullying and genocide

00:23:35.420 --> 00:23:39.510
by the Kiev regime” specially as he refers
to the language laws.

00:23:39.510 --> 00:23:40.919
This is not the case.

00:23:40.919 --> 00:23:45.340
The language laws were harsh, and that’s
why their passing to law was controversial,

00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:51.700
but they by no means are casuing a genocide
or an active eradication of Russian, or any

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:53.780
other minority language in Ukraine.

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:59.260
Russian, along with 17 other languages, is
still a recognized minority language in Ukraine

00:23:59.260 --> 00:24:05.500
and as such it can still be taught in schools,
used for plays, newspapers, music, books,

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:10.090
etc. it just can't no longer do that in place
of Ukrainian.

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:14.320
Meaning news-sites in Russian will also have
to have a Ukrainian version, schools teaching

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:19.669
Russian will have to also teach Ukrainian,
and, perhaps, most controversial “students

00:24:19.669 --> 00:24:25.169
are only given the right to study ‘the language
of the respective indigenous people’ rather

00:24:25.169 --> 00:24:27.580
than in the language of their minority”.

00:24:27.580 --> 00:24:32.580
With that said, other things like theater
shows can remain in Russian, or any other

00:24:32.580 --> 00:24:37.809
minority language, and minority language book
stores can operate just as normal.

00:24:37.809 --> 00:24:43.830
In the end, yes, the language laws are harsh,
and there was a backlash against them in Ukraine,

00:24:43.830 --> 00:24:52.679
and in neighboring countries, but they are
not “bullying and genocide by the Kiev regime”.

00:24:52.679 --> 00:24:59.390
The people who are actually oppressed the
most by the Ukrainian language laws aren’t

00:24:59.390 --> 00:25:02.690
Russians but Rusyns living in Transcarpathia
(or Ruthenia).

00:25:02.690 --> 00:25:07.710
This is because despite Rusyn being recognized
as a minority language in most Eastern European

00:25:07.710 --> 00:25:13.809
countries, in Ukraine, it is only seen as
a Ukrainian dialect and, therefore, not worthy

00:25:13.809 --> 00:25:15.610
of a minority language status.

00:25:15.610 --> 00:25:21.120
So, unlike Russian, it does not get the privileges
of publishing its own books, teaching its

00:25:21.120 --> 00:25:24.620
own classes, printing its own newspapers,
etc.

00:25:24.620 --> 00:25:30.309
As Elaine Rusinko states “Today in Ukraine,
Rusyn newspapers do not enjoy any support

00:25:30.309 --> 00:25:34.840
from the government, unlike the publications
of many other national minorities, and Rusyns

00:25:34.840 --> 00:25:39.070
are not even allowed to establish Saturday
or Sunday schools where they might be taught

00:25:39.070 --> 00:25:44.059
their own language” and culture.

00:25:44.059 --> 00:25:49.160
What is interesting here is that Putin in
his paper On the Historical Unity of Russians

00:25:49.160 --> 00:25:55.360
and Ukrainians did mention Rusyns as distinct
from Ukranians and allegedly even supports

00:25:55.360 --> 00:25:57.370
Rusyn independent movements.

00:25:57.370 --> 00:26:01.580
But all of this is purely a political play
by Putin and the goal of all Rusyn movements

00:26:01.580 --> 00:26:06.600
at the moment is not to “secede from Ukraine,
but to restore autonomous status within its

00:26:06.600 --> 00:26:09.789
framework.”

00:26:09.789 --> 00:26:16.590
In the end Ukraine is not a saint, ironically,
there are no saints in history, but all the

00:26:16.590 --> 00:26:23.760
historical statements used by Putin as propaganda
to justify the current war are, as shown,

00:26:23.760 --> 00:26:24.809
historically inaccurate.

00:26:24.809 --> 00:26:29.360
Putin’s statement of “I think that the
Russian and Ukrainian peoples are practically

00:26:29.360 --> 00:26:35.390
one single people” pedals centuries old
Russian propaganda of a unified Rus’ people

00:26:35.390 --> 00:26:42.060
despite such a thing never existing in history.

00:26:42.060 --> 00:26:46.590
To anyone who has been effected or knows people
who have been affected by the war in Ukraine

00:26:46.590 --> 00:26:51.020
and are trying to escape to neighboring countries,
in the description of this video, I have tried

00:26:51.020 --> 00:26:56.679
to give as many links and phone numbers to
Polish, Slovak, Romanian, etc. organizations

00:26:56.679 --> 00:27:00.220
that are trying to help all the Ukrainian
refugees.

00:27:00.220 --> 00:27:04.909
Hopefully this video was helpful in dispelling
some of the falsehoods outhether about the

00:27:04.909 --> 00:27:07.460
history of the Ukrainian and Russian relations.

00:27:07.460 --> 00:27:11.909
Of course, this video could not have been
all encompassing but I tried to at least address

00:27:11.909 --> 00:27:13.429
all the major points.

